00:035:37.000 --> 00:035:47.000
57, 19 times 3. Now, when you go back to Sura Q here, you notice that Q

00:035:47.000 --> 00:035:57.000
is a symbol, or stands for Quran. Q stands for Quran or Q here stands for Quran.

00:035:57.000 --> 00:036:07.000
And if you add the 57 Q of this Sura number 50, plus the 57 Qaf

00:036:07.000 --> 00:036:16.000
or Q in Sura number 42, also 57, 57 plus 57 is 114, which is exactly the same

00:036:16.000 --> 00:036:28.000
number as the Suras of Quran. 57 plus 57 equals 114, the number of Suras in Quran.

00:036:28.000 --> 00:036:35.000
You notice that the Sura Q is number 50 and it consists of 45

00:036:35.000 --> 00:036:41.000
verses. If you add the number of the Sura which is 50 to the number of verses

00:036:41.000 --> 00:036:49.000
in the Sura which is 45, the total is 95 or 19 times 5. Well, this is half the

00:036:49.000 --> 00:036:55.000
story. If you go to the only other Sura initialed with Q which is Sura number 42,

00:036:55.000 --> 00:037:02.000
you see that the number of verses is 53. And if you add the number of the Sura

00:037:02.000 --> 00:037:07.000
to the number of the verses, you get exactly the same total as Sura Q,

00:037:07.000 --> 00:037:15.000
which is 95. 42 plus 53 is 95, or 19 times 5.

00:037:15.000 --> 00:037:21.000
And with Sura Q, 50, the number of the Sura, plus the number of verses 45,

00:037:21.000 --> 00:037:30.000
50 plus 45 is 95, or 19 times 5. In this Sura, the Quran is described as Majeed.

00:037:30.000 --> 00:037:33.000
(50:1) قٓ ۚ وَٱلْقُرْءَانِ ٱلْمَجِيدِ

00:037:33.000 --> 00:037:39.000
And this word Majeed has its numerical value is 57,

00:037:39.000 --> 00:037:48.000
which is the number of the letter Q in this Sura. Majeed, the M is 30, the

00:037:48.000 --> 00:038:00.000
Jeem is 3, the Ya is 10, and the Daal is 4, and you add these numbers, 30, plus 3,

00:038:00.000 --> 00:038:08.000
plus 10, plus 4 - the total is 57, 19 times 3. When the Quran was revealed, there were

00:038:08.000 --> 00:038:14.000
no numbers. These letters were used as numbers. So, you can look at the Meem as

00:038:14.000 --> 00:038:20.000
the letter Meem or M, and also as the numeral 30. The same with the other

00:038:20.000 --> 00:038:26.000
letters. So, this is a universal established system of... where the alphabet

00:038:26.000 --> 00:038:38.000
letters are used as numbers. When we go to Sura 68, which is initialed with the

00:038:38.000 --> 00:038:48.000
letter NuN, N, if you count the letter N wherever you see it in this Sura,

00:038:48.000 --> 00:038:59.000
you find that the total is 133, 19 times 7. In the Quran, there are three

00:038:59.000 --> 00:039:12.000
Suras initialed with the letter Saad. The first one is Sura number 7.

00:039:12.000 --> 00:039:18.000
It is initialed with the letters: Alef Lam Meem Saad (A.L.M.S.). The second Sura that's initialed

00:039:18.000 --> 00:039:25.000
with this letter is Sura number 19,

00:039:25.000 --> 00:039:36.000
Sura Maryam, which has five initials: Kaf Ha Ya 'Ayn Saad. So, this is the

00:039:36.000 --> 00:039:40.000
second Sura where we see the initial, the letter Saad as an initial.

00:039:40.000 --> 00:039:49.000
The third Sura initialed with this letter is Sura number 38, which is also entitled

00:039:49.000 --> 00:040:04.000
Saad. The name of the Sura is Saad, and the initial is Saad. So, these are three

00:040:04.000 --> 00:040:08.000
Suras initialed with the letter Saad, and when you count the letter Saad in the

00:040:08.000 --> 00:040:15.000
three Suras, the total comes to 152, or 19 times 8.

00:041:46.000 --> 00:041:51.000
There is one Sura in the Quran initialed with the letters

00:041:51.000 --> 00:041:59.000
Ya Seen, two letters, Ya and Seen. It is Sura number 36. See, the first verse is

00:041:59.000 --> 00:042:06.000
the two letters Ya and Seen. And if you count these two letters, Ya and Seen in the

00:042:06.000 --> 00:042:18.000
whole Sura, the total is 285, or 19 times 15. So, you see that consistently, the

00:042:18.000 --> 00:042:24.000
Suras contain a number of their initials that is consistently a multiple

00:042:24.000 --> 00:042:37.000
of 19. There are 7 Suras initialed with the letters Ha and Meem, 7

00:042:37.000 --> 00:042:48.000
consecutive Suras, beginning at Sura number 40. See, there is Sura number

00:042:48.000 --> 00:042:57.000
40, initialed with the letters Ha Meem. The whole verse consists of just

00:042:57.000 --> 00:043:09.000
the two letters, Ha Meem, 7 consecutive Suras. This is the last one,

00:043:09.000 --> 00:043:15.000
Sura number 46. It is initialed with the letters Ha Meem.

00:043:15.000 --> 00:043:21.000
And you count these distinctive unique letters, Ha and Meem, in the seven

00:043:21.000 --> 00:043:30.000
Suras. And you find that the total is 2147, the total of Ha plus Meem in the

00:043:30.000 --> 00:043:43.000
7 Suras. This is 19 times 113, 2147. This means if only one letter Ha or one

00:043:43.000 --> 00:043:50.000
letter Meem was lost or added in the last 1400 years, the whole mathematical

00:043:50.000 --> 00:043:55.000
system collapses. But as it is, you count them right now in any Quran anywhere in

00:043:55.000 --> 00:044:03.000
the world and you find that Ha and Meem in the 7 Ha Meem initialed Suras

00:044:03.000 --> 00:044:10.000
totals 2147, or 19 times 113.

00:044:21.000 --> 00:044:30.000
Sura number 42 has two sets of initials. As you have just

00:044:30.000 --> 00:044:37.000
seen, it has the initials Ha Meem in verse one, and verse two of this Sura has the

00:044:37.000 --> 00:044:44.000
initials 'Ayn Seen Qaf, three letters, 'Ayn Seen and Qaf. And if you count these

00:044:44.000 --> 00:044:51.000
three distinct letters in this Sura, 'Ayn plus Seen plus Qaf, the total is 209

00:044:51.000 --> 00:044:58.000
or 19 times 11. Sura number 19 has the largest or the

00:044:58.000 --> 00:045:06.000
biggest set of initials. It has five letters. This is Sura number

00:045:06.000 --> 00:045:19.000
19, and it is initialed with five letters: Kaf Ha Ya 'Ayn Saad. And you add, you

00:045:19.000 --> 00:045:30.000
count these letters in this Sura, the five letters total: 798, or 19 times 42.

00:045:30.000 --> 00:045:38.000
Now, I wish to remind you that the letter Saad, for example, interacts or is

00:045:38.000 --> 00:045:43.000
interlocking with the other Saad initialed Suras, Sura number seven and

00:045:43.000 --> 00:045:48.000
Surah number 38. You remember that this letter Saad

00:045:48.000 --> 00:045:55.000
in the three Saad-initialed Suras is 152, or 19 times 8, but it also

00:045:55.000 --> 00:046:01.000
is intricately intertwined with these letters in this Sura to give us a total

00:046:01.000 --> 00:046:09.000
of 798, or 19 times 42. So, you can see that this mathematical system is far

00:046:09.000 --> 00:046:12.000
beyond human capability.

00:047:18.000 --> 00:047:23.000
There are six Suras in the Quran initialed with these letters:

00:047:23.000 --> 00:047:34.000
Alef Laam Meem, A.L.M. They are Suras number 2, 3, 29, 30, 31, and 32. This happens

00:047:34.000 --> 00:047:45.000
to be Sura number 32. And every single one of the six Suras contains a total

00:047:45.000 --> 00:047:53.000
of these letters which is a multiple of 19, every, every one. For example, Sura

00:047:53.000 --> 00:048:03.000
number 2 contains 9899 of these letters and that's a multiple 19, 19 times 521.

00:048:03.000 --> 00:048:08.000
Sura number 3 also contains a multiple of 19 of these letters:

00:048:08.000 --> 00:048:14.000
Alef Laam Meem, and so on. Every one of the six Suras contains a total of Alef

00:048:14.000 --> 00:048:18.000
plus Laam plus Meem which is a multiple of 19.

00:049:02.000 --> 00:049:05.000
There are six... there are five...

00:049:07.000 --> 00:049:10.000
There are five Suras in the Quran initialed with

00:049:10.000 --> 00:049:17.000
these three letters: Alef Laam Ra, A.L.R. And every single one of the five Suras

00:049:17.000 --> 00:049:30.000
contains a total of Alef plus Laam plus Ra, which is a multiple of 19, every one.

00:050:42.000 --> 00:050:50.000
Sura number seven is initialed with the four letters: Alef Laam Meem Saad,

00:050:50.000 --> 00:050:57.000
as you see here. And when you count these letters Alef plus Laam plus Meem plus Saad,

00:050:57.000 --> 00:051:08.000
in this Sura, the total comes to 5320 which is 19 times 280. And again, I wish

00:051:08.000 --> 00:051:14.000
to remind you that this letter Saad interlocks between this Sura and the

00:051:14.000 --> 00:051:19.000
other Saad-initialed Suras, Sura number 19 and Sura number 38, and every time

00:051:19.000 --> 00:051:23.000
within the Sura, and also with its sister Suras where the letter Saad is

00:051:23.000 --> 00:051:29.000
found, the totals are consistently a multiple of 19.

00:052:10.000 --> 00:052:21.000
Sura number 13 is initialed with the letters Alef Laam Meem Ra, four initials,

00:052:21.000 --> 00:052:29.000
Alef Laam Meem Ra. When you count these letters Alef plus Laam, plus Meem, plus Ra

00:052:29.000 --> 00:052:33.000
in this Sura, you find that the total is

00:052:33.000 --> 00:052:51.000
1482, 19 times 78. There are five Suras in the Quran initialed with the letters

00:052:51.000 --> 00:053:02.000
Ha, as we see in Sura 19 here, there's the letter Ha, one of the five initials

00:053:02.000 --> 00:053:13.000
in Sura 19. And then in Sura Ta Ha there it is, Ta Ha.

00:053:13.000 --> 00:053:30.000
And the initials Ta Seen Meem in Sura number 26 right here, Ta Seen Meem.

00:053:30.000 --> 00:053:40.000
And in Sura 27, it is the initials Ta Seen, right here. And Ta Seen Meem

00:053:40.000 --> 00:053:52.000
in Sura number 28, Ta Seen Meem. You count these letters in the 5 Suras

00:053:52.000 --> 00:054:01.000
and you find that the total is 1767, or 19 times 93.

00:054:07.000 --> 00:054:13.000
People keep asking why 19? Why did God choose the number 19 as the

00:054:13.000 --> 00:054:18.000
common denominator throughout the Quran to prove every element of the Quran?

00:054:18.000 --> 00:054:23.000
The numbers of verses, the number of Suras, the numbers of words from a certain

00:054:23.000 --> 00:054:29.000
root, the numbers of letters, the initials as you have seen, and we find

00:054:29.000 --> 00:054:35.000
the number 19 in the Quran in Sura number 74 verse number 30. We find

00:054:35.000 --> 00:054:39.000
the number 19, and we find it connected with the proof that the Quran

00:054:39.000 --> 00:054:45.000
is not human-made. Some people say the Quran is human-made.

00:054:45.000 --> 00:054:47.000
إِنْ هَـٰذَآ إِلَّا قَوْلُ ٱلْبَشَرِ (74:25)

00:054:47.000 --> 00:054:51.000
as it says in Sura number 74 verse 25. And God says the answer to

00:054:51.000 --> 00:054:58.000
these people is the number 19, as we see in verse 30 of Sura 74. Now, why 19?

00:054:58.000 --> 00:055:05.000
It turns out that 19 is God's signature on everything He created. As to the

00:055:05.000 --> 00:055:14.000
answer to the question why 19?, we discovered that 19 is the basic message

00:055:14.000 --> 00:055:23.000
of the Quran. Because 19 is the numerical value of the Arabic word ONE. So, the whole

00:055:23.000 --> 00:055:31.000
message of the Quran is God alone, God is one, worship God alone. And 19 is the

00:055:31.000 --> 00:055:37.000
numerical value of the word WAHD (one) in Arabic. When the Quran was revealed, there were

00:055:37.000 --> 00:055:41.000
no numbers. The alphabet letters were used as numbers, and the letter Wow

00:055:41.000 --> 00:055:49.000
also served as the numeral 6. The letter Alef was 1. The letter Ha was 8.

00:055:49.000 --> 00:055:57.000
And the letter Daal was 4. WAHD 6 plus 1 plus 8 plus 4, the total is 19.

00:055:57.000 --> 00:056:04.000
And this is why 19 is the common denominator throughout the Quran, proving every

00:056:04.000 --> 00:056:08.000
aspect, every element of the Quran.

